  "body": "The [guidance for markup generators](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#guidance-for-markup-generators) says:\r\n\r\n> Markup generators may specify a `generator-unable-to-provide-required-alt` attribute on `img` elements for which they have been unable to obtain alternative text and for which they have therefore omitted the `alt` attribute\\. The value of this attribute must be the empty string\\. Documents containing such attributes are not conforming, but conformance checkers will silently ignore this error\\.\r\n\r\nThis non-conformance seems very strict in terms of the generator not being _able to_ provide alternative text. Could it be an option to make `generator-unable-to-provide-required-alt` conforming, in the light of it signaling that it was not possible to provide the respective information?\r\n\r\nApart from acknowledging the impossibility of the situation, it would allow generator markup to still be valid otherwise. It could potentially also encourage tooling to do something special in the presence of this attribute (my naive interpretation).",
